    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/musical-rotary-phone"
keywords:
  - Fibonacci numbers
  - Lucas numbers
  - Zeckendorf representation
  - greedy algorithm
  - OEIS
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Let a(n) be the number of terms in the greedy representation of n by the
  Fibonacci and Lucas numbers (OEIS A214973). We prove that
  a(1) + ... + a(n) = (1/5) n log_phi n + O(n). With Lekkerkerker's theorem
  this settles Kimberling's conjecture that the ratio of the number of Zeckendorf summands of 1, ..., n
  to this sum tends to a limit in (1.2, 1.4); the limit is (5 - sqrt 5)/2.
  We also prove the conjectures of Greathouse and Kurkov on A214973. The
  proofs are formalized in Lean 4.
references:
